Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:09:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 41/59] arm64: dts: rockchip: h96-max-v58: DDR DVFS on

t3 disabled &dfi and &dmc to rule DDR DVFS out as the 6.12 freeze
cause. The freeze proved to be the Wi-Fi power GPIO (t5), and t3 froze
with both nodes off, so DDR DVFS is cleared. On 6.12 the dfi gets its
four pclk_ddr_mon clocks and the dmc probes on the box BL31 v1.28 (t2
journal: current ATF version 0x100, get_stall_time unsupported, rates
528/1560/2112 MHz from the DDR v1.08 frequency table).

Drop the two disabled overrides; rk3588-android.dtsi sets both okay
with center-supply vdd_ddr_s0 and mem-supply vdd_log_s0, and the SoC
dtsi keeps the vendor dmc_ondemand setup (auto-freq-en, upthreshold 40,
downdifferential 20, system-status levels). With auto-freq-en the idle
floor is the lowest rate; load above 40 % of DFI capacity selects the
top rate; the input boost raises it for 500 ms on key and button
events. Add delayed-freq-scaling: the dmc holds the loader rate for
30 s after probe, so no rate change falls into boot or the
h96-kernel-switch guard window.

Runtime off switch without reboot: performance governor on
/sys/class/devfreq/dmc. 6.12 dvfs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P6itje71iKPFBX7YKkfvRo
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts | 8 ++------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
index e1a9b40e2..21ec425b4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
@@ -527,13 +527,9 @@ &vop {
 	/delete-property/ vop-supply;
 };
 
-/* DDR DVFS off: on 6.1 dfi fails (no pclk_ddr_mon_ch0) and dmc never probes, DDR rate stays as set by loader */
-&dfi {
-	status = "disabled";
-};
-
+/* DDR DVFS (dfi + dmc okay from rk3588-android.dtsi); loader rate held for 30 s after probe */
 &dmc {
-	status = "disabled";
+	delayed-freq-scaling;
 };
 
 /* AV1 decoder and its IOMMU */
